Subject: a Windows claim reads the bootstrap header's process marks alone, so a client's connect is not refused TouchesWord
Why: kiln's slates_e2e drives on GitHub's Windows (runs 44784112194 microVM on windows-2025, 44784299374 bare metal on windows-latest) ended at Slates' anchor: 'the channel's shared memory refused: shared layout refused at 0 for 64 bytes: TouchesWord': unanswered_end and holder_lives copied the whole 64-byte bootstrap header, whose bytes 8-24 are declared words; slates main 721f4ff97 (A-717) copies the marks (bytes 24-48) alone; carried until kiln re-vendors at or past it

